WEBVTT

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:13.300
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.880
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.780
<i>Overlooking the rows of houses and stores</i>

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.190
<i>from the highest vantage,</i>

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:27.300
<i>Such things as tears and sadness</i>

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:31.440
<i>will quickly vanish</i>

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:37.000
<i>The birds, wind, and sunshine...</i>

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:41.190
<i>...all are your friends</i>

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.260
<i>I'll carry this dream farther than far</i>

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:51.350
<i>...no matter the distance...</i>

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:58.110
<i>I long to fly freely</i>

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:02.390
<i>through the blue sky in my heart...</i>

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:05.320
<i>The far distant blue sky</i>

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:12.770
<i>It flows into tomorrow</i>

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:25.200
Takara Fansubs

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:34.740
<i>Anzelmo had beguiled Romeo in an attempt to ensnare him.</i>

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:38.880
<i>But his plans went awry...</i>

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:43.830
<i>...and Anzelmo was run out of the Wolf Pack.</i>

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:48.300
<i>Out of hatred for Romeo, Anzelmo vowed revenge,</i>

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:53.530
<i>...and ironically placed the blame for these events on Romeo's head.</i>

00:01:55.380 --> 00:02:00.320
Episode 12:

00:01:55.380 --> 00:02:00.320
To Vanish into the City of Mists

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:16.830
Just wait, Romeo.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:19.830
I'll drive you into a pit!

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:23.260
Boss... Anzelmo's actually an okay guy, after all.

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:26.180
He told me we could be friends from now on.

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:31.580
I think we're going to get along great, the two of us!

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:36.390
Anzelmo!

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:39.780
Anzelmo! What's wrong?

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:41.900
What happened, Anzelmo?

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:44.880
It's... nothing.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.880
It damned well looks like more than "nothing"!

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.180
Imagine, walking around in broad daylight with such a hideous face!

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:54.980
Wait here a bit...
I'll go get some water.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:57.780
What happened?

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.680
It was THEM... the Wolf Pack!

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.680
Wasn't it! Anzelmo!

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:16.580
Forget about me...

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:18.190
So long as YOU made it okay...

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:20.190
What do you mean?

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:24.380
I can't tell you... if I did, it would only bring you trouble.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:26.980
Anzelmo!

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:30.180
Please, tell me what happened!

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:33.330
He said...

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:38.460
that he wants to beat you up and drive you out of town.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:40.710
Who's "he"?

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:42.460
Tachioni.

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:45.470
Tachioni...?

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:49.180
He hates strangers with a passion.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:53.470
I stopped him!
I told him we were friends!

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:56.880
But then...

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:18.080
Where is he... Tachioni?

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:19.680
The... bridge...

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:26.880
Romeo!

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:28.980
I'll be back soon, boss.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:30.780
Romeo!

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.280
Dad...

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:34.980
Water...

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:39.380
Water...

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.080
Here. Drink.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:54.480
On account of me, Anzelmo...!

00:04:58.180 --> 00:04:59.380
Hey there, oaf!

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:06.780
Where's Tachioni?

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:08.180
Say what?

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:12.180
Anzelmo got beaten black and blue for sticking up for me.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.280
Sticking up for you?!

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:18.080
I can't let it slide.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.980
Man, you sure come up with the wildest stuff to say.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:26.080
Well, Tachioni's in there, if you want him.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:27.580
Stupid! Don't TELL him!

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:34.480
So, that's where he is.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:40.880
Wait here, okay? I'll be back.
I'm going to look for Romeo.

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:10.210
If you wanted to start something with me,

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:12.210
you should have come straight off and done it!

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:22.700
Don't ever lay another finger on Anzelmo!

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:25.790
If that ever happens to him again...!

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:28.080
What if it does?

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:30.480
Perfect!

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:34.380
I was going stir-crazy having no one to punch the living daylights out of...

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:53.980
Punk!

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:00.280
Get him, Tachioni!

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:01.480
Right there!

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:05.630
Bastard!

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:15.880
Stop it!

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:18.880
This is between the two of them. Don't interfere.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:37.780
Moving around like a god-damned ballerina...

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:45.780
Okay... your little game is OVER now.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:51.750
What?! The Wolf Gang is rumbling in that boat?

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:53.980
They're always sneaking onboard.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:55.780
Okay.

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:40.630
That... hurts!

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:43.730
That's the spirit, Tachioni!
Get him! Get him!

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:49.630
This is the end!

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:51.940
Say your prayers!

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:54.270
What's going on here?

00:08:55.930 --> 00:09:00.500
It seems you fellows come onboard and steal food here pretty often lately.

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:02.130
Oh shit... run!

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:07.630
Who called for help?
Where's "Romeo"?

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:09.230
This must be him!

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:10.230
Tachioni!

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:12.130
Are you all right?

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:13.930
Yes, I'm okay.

00:09:13.930 --> 00:09:15.030
Get yourself together, then.

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:16.130
Can you stand?

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:35.400
What?! Cops found the boat?

00:09:35.690 --> 00:09:38.720
That Romeo guy planned the whole thing!

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:41.530
He warned the cops beforehand!

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:43.830
He set us up for a trap!

00:09:44.030 --> 00:09:47.160
I can't believe that guy!
Teaming up with ADULTS!

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:49.930
Damned coward!

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:00.630
What's wrong, Nikita?

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:02.230
A guy like that...

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:05.430
...why would he want to do such a thing?

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:09.030
It's Romeo's fault that we can't go in that storehouse any more, you know!

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:10.730
I guess. But...

00:10:11.030 --> 00:10:12.330
What are we going to do, Giovanni?

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:27.230
You're going to beat him into a pulp!

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:34.530
Meanwhile, Angeletta could sense trouble in the air.

00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:38.480
Anzelmo!

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:42.530
What on earth happened to you?

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:43.830
Mom!

00:10:43.930 --> 00:10:44.930
Anzelmo!

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:45.830
Mom!

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:50.230
You poor thing! Who could have done such a thing?

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:54.030
Romeo did it!

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:56.730
ROMEO did it?

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:06.830
The world turned black before Angeletta's very eyes.

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:10.430
It can't be!

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:16.930
<i>Angeletta, her heart weakened by long illness,</i>

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:19.830
<i>had been warned against too much excitement by her doctor.</i>

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:28.630
Romeo... don't come back home!

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:31.630
I just know...

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:33.430
something terrible...

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:34.730
is going to happen...

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:56.230
Now that guy will never beat up on Anzelmo again.

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:00.530
God-dammit!

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:15.930
<i>Far deeper-reaching than the bruises on Anzelmo's face were those within his heart.</i>

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:21.360
<i>Anzelmo's hatred of Romeo grew, bit by bit, all the more...</i>

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:47.330
What could I do? Romeo is go...

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:56.230
Anzelmo? What's he...?

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:18.230
Somebody! Hey! Come quick!

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:21.730
What?!

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:23.830
Anzelmo, what's wrong?

00:13:35.930 --> 00:13:36.830
What's this?

00:13:36.950 --> 00:13:38.730
Why does he have all these coins in his bag?

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:42.030
It's obvious why! He stole them!

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:43.830
Stole?

00:13:55.630 --> 00:13:57.230
It's gone, after all!

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:05.820
The money I had hidden in here, it's gone!

00:14:05.840 --> 00:14:06.710
That can't be!

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:08.460
Then -- it really was...

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:09.950
It was Romeo!

00:14:14.440 --> 00:14:15.520
Wait!

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:19.930
Wait! It's not true!

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:23.330
Angeletta!

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:28.830
...not true...

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:33.530
Angeletta! You mustn't leave your room!

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:37.830
Anzelmo was...

00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:40.430
Anz...

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:43.030
Angeletta!

00:14:44.510 --> 00:14:45.820
She's got a raging fever.

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:48.530
The doctor! Get the doctor!

00:14:56.830 --> 00:15:00.330
How am I going to explain how I got these bruises to Angeletta?

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:05.630
I guess "playing with a bear" isn't going to cut it.

00:15:09.330 --> 00:15:10.130
I'm back.

00:15:17.630 --> 00:15:20.030
S -- sorry for being late.

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:24.130
I knew you wouldn't run away.

00:15:24.130 --> 00:15:26.130
I was positive you'd come back...

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:28.830
...to get the things you had stolen!

00:15:29.730 --> 00:15:31.030
Things I'd stolen?

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:36.130
You dirty little thief!

00:15:42.630 --> 00:15:44.430
What the hell were you gonna do with it?!

00:15:45.030 --> 00:15:47.730
Were you planning on splitting it up between your Wolf Pack friends?

00:15:48.930 --> 00:15:50.530
What are you talking about?

00:15:51.730 --> 00:15:53.430
Stop playing the fool.

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:55.730
We found this in your bag!

00:15:57.730 --> 00:16:00.030
I don't know anything about it!

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:05.280
You got your Wolf Pack to gang up on Anzelmo and beat him up, eh?!

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:12.030
Piccolo!

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:16.230
Stop it, Piccolo!

00:16:17.230 --> 00:16:18.330
Hey!

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:24.630
Is that devil yours?

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:27.030
Piccolo isn't a devil!

00:16:27.530 --> 00:16:30.330
Boss, please listen to what I have to say. I...

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:33.330
I thought there was some good in you.

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:36.530
But God! What a mistake that was!

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:39.530
You're nothing but a godforsaken packrat thief!

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:43.130
I can't let you stay here any longer.

00:16:43.430 --> 00:16:47.130
Anzelmo, lock him up until the police get here!

00:16:47.430 --> 00:16:48.730
Yes, Dad.

00:16:56.130 --> 00:16:58.730
Police?! Why are the police coming?

00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:01.030
I haven't done anything!

00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:07.830
Anzelmo...

00:17:08.030 --> 00:17:10.030
...you believe me, don't you?

00:17:17.230 --> 00:17:18.830
Angeletta said she couldn't believe it.

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:21.330
That you were a thief.

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:23.830
She felt betrayed, she said.

00:17:37.630 --> 00:17:39.730
Farewell, Romeo.

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:53.270
The police will be here soon to take that good-for-nothing off to prison.

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:56.320
Then it's the whip for him, or an island exile.

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:03.530
I don't want to see his face again!

00:18:04.880 --> 00:18:07.670
Oh well. Now I'm going to have to look for a new kid.

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:13.530
Romeo...

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:14.340
Romeo...!

00:18:20.310 --> 00:18:21.830
Angeletta...

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:23.720
I'll never see you again.

00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:27.030
And I'll have left you with nothing but contempt for me!

00:18:28.220 --> 00:18:29.530
Prison!

00:18:38.110 --> 00:18:38.980
Alfredo!

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:42.430
What would you do if you were in my place?

00:18:53.300 --> 00:18:55.120
The policeman is here.

00:18:56.380 --> 00:18:58.500
He's inside.

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:05.300
Be sure to whip him. Give him at least ten floggings.

00:19:05.460 --> 00:19:07.270
Ten floggings isn't severe enough.

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:11.710
The only way to "teach" incorrigible boys like this is through their hide.

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:20.190
One kid from a while ago went and passed OUT on us 'cause we whipped him so much.

00:19:58.430 --> 00:19:59.430
Anzelmo...

00:19:59.730 --> 00:20:01.030
You..!

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:05.630
Romeo got away!

00:20:39.530 --> 00:20:43.160
You're not getting away this time, you coward.

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:32.930
Get him!

00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:35.290
Let's beat this jerk into a bloody pulp!

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:58.140
<i>The wolf-pack moves in for the kill!</i>

00:21:58.430 --> 00:22:02.310
<i>And right at the last moment
-- a masked boy appears.</i>

00:22:02.780 --> 00:22:04.530
<i>Is... is it you?</i>

00:22:04.690 --> 00:22:07.430
<i>It's an unexpected reunion.</i>

00:22:07.980 --> 00:22:11.690
See you then!

00:22:07.980 --> 00:22:11.690
<i>Reunion in the Sewer</i>

00:22:07.980 --> 00:22:11.690
Next time:

00:22:13.110 --> 00:22:17.010
<i>"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"</i>

00:22:25.780 --> 00:22:29.880
<i>Si Si Ciao, why do the good times</i>

00:22:29.980 --> 00:22:34.180
<i>seem to end so soon?</i>

00:22:34.380 --> 00:22:38.380
<i>Si Si Ciao, we're all friends</i>

00:22:38.580 --> 00:22:42.580
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>

00:22:43.190 --> 00:22:47.490
<i>Your laughing voice dances</i>

00:22:47.490 --> 00:22:51.390
<i>Once again in the sky</i>

00:22:51.790 --> 00:22:58.690
<i>Your pocket bursting with memories</i>

00:23:00.390 --> 00:23:04.290
<i>Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now</i>

00:23:04.490 --> 00:23:08.490
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>
